 cfg←ReadPackageConfig packagePath;qdmx
⍝ Returns the config of the package in `packagePath` as a namespace. `packagePath` may also be
⍝ the name of the config file itself.
⍝ When the config cannot be read the result is an empty namespace, so that every field simply
⍝ reads as missing: a page can do without the config, and one that cannot be read is no reason
⍝ to break the page. It is logged, though.
 :Trap 11 19 22 Reg.ErrorNo
     cfg←Reg.GetPackageConfigFileAsNS packagePath
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     cfg←⎕NS''
     LogError'Cannot read the package config in "',packagePath,'": ',qdmx.EM,'; RC=',⍕qdmx.EN
 :EndTrap
